Project Overview
MindOS is designed as a private digital workspace.

The application currently contains the following areas:

Section	Purpose
Dashboard	Application overview
Mind	Capture and record mental state
Thoughts	Store personal thoughts
Focus	Track focus sessions
Filter	Separate thoughts into useful categories
Reprogram	Create and complete intentional routines
Explore	Explore questions and ideas
Settings	Manage user profile and preferences

The application uses authentication so each user's data can be associated with their account.

Features
Authentication
MindOS supports:

User registration

User login

Password hashing

JWT authentication

Protected API routes

User-specific data

Passwords are never stored as plain text.

Passwords are hashed using bcryptjs.

Authentication tokens are generated using jsonwebtoken.

Mind
The Mind section allows users to record:

Energy

Clarity

Stress

Mood

Notes

Each entry belongs to the authenticated user.

Thoughts
Users can create and manage personal thoughts.

A thought can contain:

Content

Mood

Creation time

Updated time

Users only access their own thoughts.

Focus
Focus sessions can be created and tracked.

The backend stores information associated with the user's focus sessions.

Filter
The Filter section helps organize thoughts into categories such as:

Thought

Category

Reality

Action

Reprogram
Users can create intentional routines or affirmations.

A reprogram entry contains:

Title

Description

Affirmation

Completion status

Completion timestamp

Users can mark a reprogram entry as completed or incomplete.

Explore
The Explore section is intended to provide a space for exploring:

Questions

Problems

Ideas

Useful information

AI functionality can be integrated here in a future version.

