Application Architecture
The current application follows a three-tier architecture.

                   User
                    |
                    v
             React Frontend
                    |
                    | HTTP API
                    v
             Node.js Backend
                    |
                    | MySQL connection
                    v
                MySQL DB

For production, the intended architecture is:

                    Internet
                       |
                       v
             Application Load Balancer
                       |
             +---------+---------+
             |                   |
             v                   v
        Frontend ECS        Backend ECS
          Fargate             Fargate
                                 |
                    +------------+------------+
                    |                         |
                    v                         v
              Secrets Manager            RDS MySQL

Authentication
Authentication uses JWT.

The authentication flow is:

User
 |
 | email + password
 v
POST /api/auth/login
 |
 v
Backend
 |
 | verify password
 v
JWT token
 |
 v
Frontend
 |
 | Authorization: Bearer <token>
 v
Protected API

Signup flow:

User
 |
 | name + email + password
 v
POST /api/auth/signup
 |
 v
Password hashed with bcrypt
 |
 v
User stored in MySQL
 |
 v
JWT generated

Database
The application uses MySQL.

The backend connects through:

backend/src/config/database.js

The application creates the required database tables during initialization.

The main tables are:

users
thoughts
mind_entries
focus_sessions
filters
reprograms

