Terraform Deployment
Terraform will manage the AWS infrastructure.

The planned infrastructure includes:

AWS VPC
├── Public Subnets
│   ├── Application Load Balancer
│   └── NAT Gateway
│
├── Private Subnets
│   ├── ECS Frontend
│   ├── ECS Backend
│   └── RDS MySQL
│
├── ECR
│   ├── MindOS Frontend
│   └── MindOS Backend
│
├── Secrets Manager
│   ├── Database credentials
│   └── JWT secret
│
└── CloudWatch
    └── Application logs

Terraform state should be stored remotely rather than committed to Git.

Recommended production setup:

S3
 |
 +-- Terraform state

with state locking enabled using the AWS-supported locking mechanism configured for the Terraform version being used.

Terraform Workflow
Initialize:

terraform init

Format:

terraform fmt -recursive

Validate:

terraform validate

Create a plan:

terraform plan

Apply:

terraform apply

Destroy infrastructure:

terraform destroy

Always review:

terraform plan

before applying infrastructure changes to a shared or production environment.

Security Practices
The project follows these principles:

Secrets
Do not commit:

.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials
AWS access keys
database passwords
JWT secrets

Use:

AWS Secrets Manager

for production secrets.

Database
MySQL should not be publicly accessible.

Production architecture:

Internet
   |
   X
 RDS

Instead:

Internet
   |
   v
ALB
   |
   v
Backend ECS
   |
   v
Private RDS

Network Security
Security groups should follow least privilege.

Expected traffic:

Internet
   |
   v
ALB : 80/443
   |
   v
ECS : application port
   |
   v
RDS : 3306

RDS port 3306 should only be accessible from the backend security group.

JWT
JWT secrets must be stored outside source code.

Development:

.env

Production:

AWS Secrets Manager

Git Ignore
The following should not be committed:

node_modules/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
terraform/.terraform/
terraform/*.tfstate
terraform/*.tfstate.*
terraform/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.log

Do not ignore .terraform.lock.hcl if you want Terraform provider versions to be reproducible; instead, commit the lock file.

A production repository should therefore keep:

.terraform.lock.hcl

under version control.

